@* AppShell's Asides page, moved from its Overview: an aside in the layout, a page's own panel, and
   one that is a drawer on phones. *@

<Heading Level="2">An aside</Heading>
<TextBlock>An aside is a column on the side opposite the sidebar, such as an outline of the page. Add an <Code>AppAside</Code> to the shell. For an outline, put an <Anchor Href="docs/components/on-this-page">OnThisPage</Anchor> in it, which lists the main area's headings from the server.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Aside</Code>
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem>The aside shows from its <Code>Breakpoint</Code> up, 1024px by default.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>It's <Code>Width</Code> wide, 15rem by default.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>Its content stays in view while the page scrolls, and scrolls on its own when it's taller than the window.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>When the aside holds something other than an outline, give it a <Code>Label</Code>, such as "Details". The label names its landmark for screen readers.</ListItem>
</List>
<TextBlock>The <Anchor Href="demos/app-shell/docs-outline">docs demo</Anchor> has an outline beside an article.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">A panel for the chosen row</Heading>
<TextBlock>A page can have a panel of its own in the aside column, such as the details of the row chosen in a table. Write an <Code>AppAside</Code> in the page, inside <Code>AppMain</Code>. It fills the shell's aside column, in place of the layout's aside if there is one, and pages without one leave no column.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="app-shell-detail-panel" WidthSwitch />
<TextBlock>To show the panel under the main area below its breakpoint, rather than hide it, set <Code>SmallScreen="AsideSmallScreen.Below"</Code>.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>Keep the chosen row in the URL, such as <Code>?rule=</Code>. Link each row to it with the <Anchor Href="docs/components/table">Table</Anchor>'s <Code>RowHref</Code>, and mark the chosen row with <Code>RowCurrent</Code>. The panel, and its <Anchor Href="docs/components/tabs">TabLinks</Anchor>, then work with <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">JavaScript off</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>The page's aside moves into the shell only when the page and the layout use the same render mode. A page that is interactive on its own, in a static layout, keeps the aside where it's written: a full-width block in the main area, at every width.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">A panel that opens as a drawer</Heading>
<TextBlock>An aside can be a column on wide screens and a drawer from the end side on narrow ones. Set <Code>SmallScreen="AsideSmallScreen.Drawer"</Code>, and add an <Code>AsideToggle</Code> to open it. The toggle shows only while there's a drawer to open, so it can stay in the header on every page.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="app-shell-aside-drawer" WidthSwitch />
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem>The drawer closes with its close button, a tap beside it, or Escape. Focus then returns to the toggle.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>Any link to the aside's id opens it too, with JavaScript off as well. The id is <Code>ib-aside</Code>, or the aside's <Code>Id</Code> when you set one.</ListItem>
</List>

@code {
    private const string Aside = """
        <AppShell>
            ...
            <AppMain>@Body</AppMain>
            <AppAside>
                <OnThisPage />
            </AppAside>
        </AppShell>
        """;
}
